    "STAT_CONTEXT": 5,
    "STAT_COMPLEXITY": 1,
    "OT_VERSE_REF": "Psalm 103:13",
    "OT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "As a father has compassion on his children, so the Lord has compassion on those who fear him.",
    "NT_VERSE_REF": "Matthew 7:11",
    "NT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "How much more will your Father in heaven give good gifts to those who ask him!",
    "OT_VERSE_LINE": "Psalm 103:13 — “As a father has compassion on his children, so the Lord has compassion on those who fear him.”",
    "NT_VERSE_LINE": "Matthew 7:11 — “How much more will your Father in heaven give good gifts to those who ask him!”",
    "GREEK": "Πατήρ",
    "GREEK_TRANSLIT": "Patēr",
    "HEBREW": "אָב",
    "HEBREW_TRANSLIT": "Av",
    "OT_REFS": "Psa 68:5 • Isa 9:6 • Isa 64:8 • Jer 31:9",
    "NT_REFS": "Mat 6:9 • Rom 8:15 • Gal 4:6 • Eph 4:6",
    "TRIVIA_BULLETS": [
      "The Aramaic term 'Abba' expresses deep intimacy, similar to 'Daddy' or 'Papa.'",
      "God is called 'Father' over 165 times in the Gospels, but only rarely in the Old Testament.",
      "In ancient Hebrew culture, the father was the head of the 'bet ab' and responsible for spiritual instruction."
